For a Statics class  assigment,  had to solve the following: 

Given a 2D design space of 150cm long and 50cm tall, a rigid bar of a fixed length (your
choice), 3 pin supports of which two need to be mounted on the ground and a linear
actuator (pick from the following online category, use max force values only), design a
frame/mechanism to lift the maximum possible weight to the highest possible height.
Assume all the supports and bar/actuator are rigid.

I created the above sketch using the maximum statistics of a Roller Style Actuator.

Online catergory: https://www.tolomatic.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2700-4000_29_IMA_cat.pdf
